# Project Rules
When applying this rule prefix your response with [Project Manager]

## Project Overview
- Technology stack based on Next.js 15 with TypeScript
- Follow established project architecture patterns
- Maintain consistency with existing codebase conventions

## Key Technologies
- **Next.js 15**: App Router, React Server Components
- **TypeScript**: Strict typing across all layers
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (default choice)

## Important Guidelines
1. **DO NOT reinvent existing functionality** - Use built-in features, auth, and established patterns
2. **Kill existing dev servers before builds** when needed:
   ```bash
   lsof -ti:3000 | xargs kill -9 && lsof -ti:5555 | xargs kill -9
   ```
3. **Respect project structure**:
   - `app/` - Next.js App Router pages/components
   - `app/(authenticated)/` - Auth-required pages (if applicable)
   - `app/(public)/` - Public pages (if applicable)
   - `app/auth/` - Authentication pages (if applicable)
   - `app/api/` - Server-side API routes
   - `components/` - Reusable UI components
   - `lib/` - Shared utilities and helpers
   - `types/` - TypeScript type definitions
   - `__tests__/` or `tests/` - Test files

## Development Workflow
- Use established development commands
- Follow existing code formatting and linting rules
- Maintain test coverage for new features
- Use TypeScript strictly - avoid `any` types

## Architecture Patterns
- Server Components by default, Client Components when needed
- API routes for server-side logic
- Proper separation of concerns
- Follow established authentication patterns
- Use appropriate state management solutions

## AI Model Preferences (if applicable)
- OpenAI: Use established model configuration
- Follow API abstraction patterns
- Implement proper error handling and rate limiting
